# Own-wording Tome of Heroes magic items, chunk B (Gazing Hydrangea to Ninefold Swarmdagger).
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}; GEAR = []
MASTERY = {}
WDESC = {}

def add(name, typ, rar, att, text, **o):
    ITEMS.append((name, typ, rar, att, text, o))

_W = "Worts are the magical herbs of Tome of Heroes. Each plant has a Minor Wort anyone can use, a Ceremony Wort that needs a ritual and a number of cuttings, and a Cultivated Wort that appears in a garden grown for the stated time. "

add("Gazing Hydrangea", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: unbinding, mental protection, psychic strength. Found in desert oases, near theaters and stages, and outside windows that face mirrors. A small shrub with short, broad leaves and hemispherical flower bundles, tiny blooms in the center and larger pink, blue and purple ones around the edge. **Minor Wort.** As an action, crush and toss petals at one creature you can see within 10 feet. It makes a Charisma save or loses attunement to one item it carries or wears, chosen at random. **Ceremony Wort.** Spend 1 hour making a flower crown from blooms and stems. While worn, the creature has Resistance to Psychic damage and its thoughts are hidden from spells such as detect thoughts. Each crown needs 2 cuttings and lasts 8 hours. **Cultivated Wort (4th level).** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks aids fortune telling and foresight. A divination spell cast there as a ritual needs no components and has double duration.")
add("Giantstrike Cestus", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 1, "Leather hand wraps fitted with iron plates engraved with runes. When you make unarmed strikes while wearing them, your Martial Arts die is one die size larger. Requires attunement by a monk.", by="Monk")
add("Greater Potion Belt", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "A plain brown leather belt with bands of flexible pale blue crystal. As an action, pour a potion onto a band, which absorbs it and turns deep blue. Each band holds one potion. This belt has three bands. While wearing it, use a bonus action to speak its command word and a stored potion's name to gain that potion's benefits as if you had drunk it.")
add("Hoary Valerian", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, _W + "Themes: dreams private and shared, relaxation, sleep. Found at campsites, near forest altars, and where enchantments were cast. A tall flowering plant with narrow paired leaves along frond-like stalks and tiny flowers bunched at the ends of side stems. **Minor Wort.** As an action, crush a sprig's leaves and blow them at a creature you can see within 10 feet. It makes a Constitution save or falls Unconscious for 1d10 minutes. The effect ends if it takes damage or someone uses an action to wake it. **Ceremony Wort (9th level).** Steep the roots in a pot of hot water for 1 minute, then pour the liquid in a ring of radius up to 20 feet. Small valerian bushes sprout and grow along the ring over 10 minutes and last 4 hours. A creature that rests inside finishes a long rest in 4 hours instead of 8 and regains twice as many Hit Dice at its end. Needs 4 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort.** A garden grown for 4 weeks gives humanoids who sleep within 1 mile shared, lucid dreams at least weekly. The dreams are usually about ordinary, peaceful life, with occasional minor prophecy.")
add("Javelin of Teleportation", "Weapon", "Uncommon", 0, "Any javelin. A short-hafted javelin with a long metal head. You have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with this magic weapon. When you hit a creature with it, you can speak its command word to force the target to make a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure, the target teleports to an unoccupied space you can see within 60 feet of you, which must be on the ground or a floor. Once used, you cannot use this property again until the next dawn. Until then it still works as a magic weapon.", fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1}, base=["Javelin"], ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
add("Knight-Sergeant's Surcoat", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1, "A long padded tabard of durable canvas and fine silk, bearing the colors and heraldry of a long-forgotten order of knights. While wearing it, you have Advantage on Animal Handling checks with horses, and on Persuasion checks with humanoids of higher social rank than yours, such as an army's general or a region's monarch. **Knight's Livery.** While attuned to and wearing both this surcoat and the argent mantle, your Charisma score is 20. It does nothing if your Charisma is already 20 or higher.")
add("Medic's Sash", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1, "While wearing this sash, your carrying capacity doubles, and your movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks if you are carrying a friendly creature at 0 hit points or dying. **First Aid.** The sash has 3 charges. While wearing it, spend 1 charge as an action to cast spare the dying, or 2 charges as an action to cast cure wounds, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (minimum +1). It regains all spent charges at dawn.", ch=[3, "3", "dawn"])
add("Memento Mori", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1, "While you have the memento mori with you, you need no food, drink or sleep. As an action, draw on all its stored memory at once to gain the effects of a potion of heroism. When the effect ends, the memento mori loses its magic. Requires attunement by the shade for whom it was offered.")
add("Merchant's Mint", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: abundance, communication, honorable deals. Found in caravan tracks, near grain silos, and where treaties were signed. A low, sprawling plant with square stems, paired serrated leaves, and flower clusters on narrow cones in white to purple. **Minor Wort.** As an action, put a sprig under your tongue and cast comprehend languages on yourself. The sprig must stay in your mouth, and the spell ends if you spit it out. **Ceremony Wort.** When you and another creature are at odds, write both names on a page, wrap it with two sprigs, and burn the bundle to summon a pseudodragon as a draconic arbitrator, or a pact drake (see Creature Codex). It hears both sides to find a friendly solution, defends itself against hostile creatures and otherwise takes no actions. It speaks Common and Draconic and stays until the dispute is resolved, up to 1 hour. The GM may let it leave early if summoned somewhere very dangerous or if the parties plainly do not want resolution. Needs 2 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort.** A garden grown for at least 12 weeks guards nearby land from disease and famine. Within 5 miles, fields never turn barren, harvests are always abundant, and livestock never fall ill from grazing.")
add("Mirthy Hops", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: joy, fellowship, humor. Found near wheat fields, at campsites, and outside drinking halls and taverns. A tall climbing vine with dark green heart-shaped leaves and fragrant pale green flower cones of overlapping petals. **Minor Wort.** As an action, eat a bud to triple your jump distance for 1 minute. Your jumping looks haphazard, and a creature that sees it makes a Wisdom save or bursts into giggles until the start of your next turn, with Disadvantage on its next attack roll or skill check. On a success it is immune to this effect for 24 hours. **Ceremony Wort (11th level).** Spend 1 minute singing a drinking song over a pitcher of ale with hop buds floating in it to call on the fey. At the end you summon a fey creature as if you had cast conjure fey. Unless harm is about to befall you or the fey, it demands you play a drinking game with it before obeying commands or agreeing to service. The GM sets the game by the fey. Needs 3 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort.** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks defends the land from overwhelming terror. Each creature within 1 mile has Advantage on saves against Frightened and Disadvantage on Intimidation checks.")
add("Nimbus Daffodil", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, _W + "Themes: change, cycle of the seasons, weather. Found at the bottom of waterfalls, near puddles after rain, and along riverbanks. A flowering plant with a branching central stem from a bulb, long narrow leaves, and a drooping two-layered trumpet flower in yellow and white. **Minor Wort.** As an action, snap a stem in two to create a 20-foot-radius sphere of fog centered on you, otherwise like fog cloud. **Ceremony Wort (6th level).** Spend 10 minutes dancing outdoors holding a wand of bundled daffodils to summon rain. The cloud is a cylinder 10 feet tall with a 120-foot radius, centered on a point you can see 100 feet directly above you. For 1 minute, plants there are watered, open containers fill with fresh water, and a spell cast in the area that creates or controls water, clouds or weather has its range or duration (caster's choice) doubled. The caster must be in the rain's area, though the spell's effect need not be, and must still keep Concentration if required. If you use your action to dance and four other creatures of level 6 or higher, each holding a daffodil wand, use a Reaction to dance with you, the rain appears on Initiative count 20 of the next round without the full 10 minutes. Needs 3 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort (7th level).** A garden grown for 5 weeks shields the area from bad weather. Within 5 miles, skies are rarely overcast, sunlight is gentle and warm, and light rain or snow falls each morning when the season suits. The gentle sun still harms creatures hurt by sunlight, like vampires.")
add("Ninefold Swarmdagger", "Weapon", "Rare", 0, "Any dagger. You have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with this magic weapon. It has 6 charges. When you hit a creature with it, use a bonus action to launch ghostly duplicate daggers at up to three creatures you can see within 30 feet of the creature you hit. Make a ranged attack with the dagger against each target. On a hit, a target takes 1d4 Force damage. After you hit six creatures with the ghostly daggers, you cannot launch more until the next dawn.", fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1}, base=["Dagger"], ch=[6, "6", "dawn"])

SP["Medic's Sash"] = {"sp": [["Spare the Dying", 1], ["Cure Wounds", 2]]}
